5.text:
The Tonga flag geometry consists of a solid red field plus a white canton rectangle containing a red cross (union of one horizontal rectangle and one vertical rectangle). This yields exactly four white rectangles inside the canton. The matrix \(M\) admits the decomposition \(M=aJ+(b-a)W\) where \(J\) has rank 1 and \(W\) is the 0-1 white indicator matrix, so \(\operatorname{rank}(M)\le1+\operatorname{rank}(W)\).  

